    "answer": "I'd recommend leaning into the current \"Moonlit Meadow\" night mood and making it feel more magical and alive, since the base is already nicely set up. Here are three directions depending on what you're after:\n\n**1. Cuter / cozier (soft pastel night)** — keep the runner and physics, warm up the palette, and add a gentle firefly ambience.\n\n**2. More atmospheric / dramatic** — deepen the night sky, add a subtle falling-stars weather effect, and a moon with rays.\n\n**3. More playful / dynamic** — switch to a flying version (real hold-to-fly mechanics), so Coco glides over the meadow instead of just jumping.\n\nMy top pick would be **#1**, because it preserves everything you have while making it noticeably cuter:\n\n- Soft pastel night gradient sky\n- Gentle fireflies drifting in the meadow\n- A warm glowing moon with rays\n- Keep Coco, the log/mushroom/moth obstacles, and the run physics exactly as they are\n\nWant me to apply that, or would you prefer one of the other directions (or a mix)?",
